    postmask_missingness_above_50pct = YES — prioritize these for investigation. This is a warning flag, not an automatic exclusion rule.
    missing_GT_fraction_after — compare values within each species/group. Look for samples substantially higher than their group, especially if they were already high before masking. This is the main measure for deciding which samples need attention.
    fraction_original_complete_GT_masked — shows the share of previously complete genotypes made missing by DP/GQ masking, basically how much of the sample’s previously complete data failed DP/GQ thresholds.
    increase_missingness_percentage_points — highlights how much masking changed missingness. A large increase may indicate low or missing DP/GQ across many calls.

